  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Suppose 10% of ball bearings produced at a factory are defective. If ten ball bearings are tested, find the probability that exactly one is defective. Give your answer in the form $a^9$ for some real number $0<a<1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\left(\\frac{9}{10}\\right)^9$",
      "worked": "Let $X$ count the defective bearings. Using $n=10$ and $p=\\frac{1}{10}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\Pr(X=1)&=\\binom{10}{1}\\left(\\frac{1}{10}\\right)\\left(\\frac{9}{10}\\right)^9\\\\\n\\Pr(X=1)&=10\\left(\\frac{1}{10}\\right)\\left(\\frac{9}{10}\\right)^9\\\\\n\\Pr(X=1)&=\\left(\\frac{9}{10}\\right)^9.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThus $a=\\frac{9}{10}$, which satisfies $0<a<1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
